ck down too  stringently in the future so  if you like the idea is that as the  cases start to tick up there's  concerns that it could lead to  exponential growth the r rate is  increasing and so actually acting early  would mean that we wouldn't have to  have the heavy fist of another national  lockdown in the future  look i think that underpins a  fundamental misunderstanding of what  happens with community  pathogens whatever you do if you lock  down now you slow down the progression  slightly  but then you'll get a resurgence because  what happens is in in the population is  there has to be a level of immunity  for this to become manageable so a very  good example of this will be older  if you go and look at oldham data today  on august the second they had a  resurgence of cases  came in hard restrictive measures more  testing tracing  but actually in the last week now they  now have the highest case numbers  they've had it in the last eight weeks  so this is the problem what we do need  to do is create a test and trace system  that's highly effective let that work  and what you're seeing amongst the  population is a single message that is  now missing  is if you have symptoms you have to  isolate  and i'm picking up a lot of people who  just do not understand that  because we haven't been clear about that  messaging and this is incredibly  important  it's become so confusing people think if  you've got the rule of six  they can go about even if they've got  symptoms so we need to clarify  and make the messaging very simple for  the population  and if we do that we can go through the  winter highly vigilant  and not need lockdown um you it's  interesting they talk about the  messaging and some of the confusion  around it  in the mail on sunday today you've said  that the prime minister is surrounded by  mediocre scientific advisors what do you  mean by that what mistakes are they  making  well one of the problems here is this is  a  pathogen that affects healthc